    "original_text": "ASTIS authored actual Gibbs gradient mean-zero sufficient background, used to recover the literal source posterior-gradient identity.\n{E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {U : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} (hα : 0 < α) (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, (α : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x v v ∧\n      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x v v ≤ (β : ℝ)*‖v‖^2) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -U x)\n    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧ Integrable (gradient U) μ ∧\n      (∫ x, gradient U x ∂μ) = 0",
    "text_sha256": "138fba8cb017d54057cdff6fb830c03ef060f906eaa51cdf2d3f36037c30ed25"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.GibbsGradientMean.integrable_gradient_and_integral_eq_zero",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Analysis/GibbsGradientMean.lean",
    "statement": "{E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {U : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} (hα : 0 < α) (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, (α : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x v v ∧\n      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x v v ≤ (β : ℝ)*‖v‖^2) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -U x)\n    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧ Integrable (gradient U) μ ∧\n      (∫ x, gradient U x ∂μ) = 0",
    "statement_sha256": "f6ef74d420c7bc7e42cbca50d07c997e999ffdb6d9c86f39ea49f472bb99b6df",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "The measure volume is the canonical Haar/Lebesgue measure for the given finite real Hilbert structure. Dimension zero is allowed.",
      "Measure.tilted normalizes exp(f) against its base measure when integrable; otherwise it is the zero measure. Probability is a conclusion here, not an assumed property of the tilt.",
      "gradient is the real Hilbert Riesz representative of the Frechet derivative. All displayed integrals are genuine Bochner integrals; integrability is a proved output.",
      "The nonnegative curvature constants may be unordered. The theorem does not assume alpha<=beta; dimension zero also permits alpha>beta."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "runs/20261007-companion-priority/smoothed-score-posterior/focused.tests.4.log PASS3751, standard3 only; local compilation only."
